OSK upstream source
===================

OSK (osk/) is GTK 4's rendering engine as an OTK module.  Imported from GTK 4.24.0:

  https://download.gnome.org/sources/gtk/4.24/gtk-4.24.0.tar.xz
  sha256 28ba4ac1c04f86eac09b79a163cb163a4c2b54442d9f7eccc04679062a581044

The commits "osk: import GTK 4.24.0 rendering engine" and "osk: import GtkSnapshot
from GTK 4.24.0" add the imported files unmodified, at the same paths as in GTK
(osk/gsk/... is GTK's gsk/...).  Every OSK change is a later commit, so

  git diff <GtkSnapshot import commit> -- osk/

shows what OSK changed.  To take a newer GTK: copy the same files from the new
release onto the import commits' tree in a branch, commit, and merge that branch.

OSK-specific changes in imported files are marked "OSK:" in comments.

